  Decoded from this project's own Figma source rather than fetched or redrawn:
  design/RadioMyata.fig -> node 2523:135 (settings-lastfm > Not connected >
  "Vector"), whose fill geometry is blob 50338 - 571 bytes, 27 path commands,
  bounds exactly 0..17.676 x 0..11. The same mark appears at 2523:115 (the
  Settings row) and 2523:133 (the Connected card); all three are one shape drawn
  in two tints, so one drawable serves them.

  ## Why the viewport is 24 and the mark is not

  The mark's intrinsic size is 17.676 x 11 - a wide wordmark, not a square icon.
  Centring it in a 24x24 viewport is a translate of (3.162, 6.5), which lands it
  at (19.16, 24.50) inside the card and (19.16, 26.50) inside the Settings row.
  The frozen frames put it at (19, 24) and (19, 26). So padding it to 24 lets it
  drop into the same 24dp slot every other Settings row uses and reproduces both
  frozen placements to within half a pixel, instead of needing its own geometry.

  ## Tint

  Deliberately no android:tint here. The mark is text_secondary when disconnected
  and primary when connected, and that is a fact about the state, not about the
  asset - so it is set at the call site.
-->
